index b52fa6d..34dbdb0 100644
--- a/docs/guides/admin-cms.md
+++ b/docs/guides/admin-cms.md
@@ -441,3 +441,16 @@ authorization and privileged operations on the server; components call those
 endpoints and present their results. Follow the [full-stack lessons](../fullstack/index.md)
 and [Teloce integration reference](../api/teloce.md) to connect this capability
 to pages, components and application modules.
+
+## CMS authorization boundary
+
+CMS denies requests when no authentication backend is configured. Mount it
+with `CMS(app, auth=admin.auth)`. The explicit `allow_unauthenticated=True`
+option is only for isolated demonstrations.
+
+Use `strict_permissions=True` for new Admin installations. Creating or changing
+content into `approved`, `scheduled`, or `published`, editing already protected
+content, scheduling it, importing protected records, publishing/unpublishing,
+and executing custom CMS actions require `cms.publish_content`. Restoring a
+revision additionally requires `cms.restore_revision` and the model change
+permission. Configure exact model permissions for editor/publisher roles.
